# E6-T3 systemd --user scheduled-reconciliation example (OPS-007).
# Install for the current user:
#   cp jjukkumi-reconcile.service jjukkumi-reconcile.timer ~/.config/systemd/user/
#   systemctl --user daemon-reload
#   systemctl --user enable --now jjukkumi-reconcile.timer
# Replace /usr/local/bin/jjukkumi and wiki-maintenance with the installed
# binary path and route id. Before the production gate the recipe omits
# --submit (persisted decisions only); after the gate add --submit to
# ExecStart.
[Unit]
Description=JJUKKUMI scheduled daily reconciliation (no daemon; one-shot CLI)
Documentation=file:/usr/local/share/doc/jjukkumi/runbook.md

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/jjukkumi reconcile --route wiki-maintenance --reason scheduled --output json
# StateDirectory is not used: the state dir comes from the configuration
# (configuration-spec s3) and stays owned by the operator.
NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=true
